ibution patterns, some members of the DEAD box protein family are believed to be involved in embryogenesis, spermatogenesis, and cellular growth and division. The function of this gene product which is a member of this family, has not been determined. Alternatively spliced transcript variants have been found for this gene. [provided by RefSeq, Jun 2010].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q9H5Z1","text":"Acts as a co-sensor in RIGI-mediated antiviral innate immunity (PubMed:39037956). Enhances RIGI recognition of viral nucleic acids and interacts with RIGI and MAVS to form a signaling complex which triggers downstream signaling cascades that lead to the induction of type I interferons and pro-inflammatory cytokines during the antiviral innate immune response (PubMed:39037956)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}